Audio Unit: own the preset names the host hands over and gets back.

AudioUnitProperties.h, kAudioUnitProperty_PresentPreset: "the client of the audio
unit owns the CFString when it retrieves the preset with PresentPreset and is
expected to release this". DPF copied the AUPreset both ways without a CFRetain:

- setting a user preset kept the host's name without a reference, so once the
  host released its own the name was freed, and the next ClassInfo put the freed
  string in the state dictionary. Logic sets a user preset for its own patches,
  then reads ClassInfo: EXC_BAD_ACCESS in PluginAU::retrieveClassInfo
  (sq8l-revival/SQ8L#37);
- getting PresentPreset gave the host a reference it did not have, which the
  host's release then took from the plug-in's own name.

Also refuse a factory preset number past the end, and ignore one in a saved
state, instead of reading past the end of the preset table.

